# Running commands

Work from the repository root unless a command says otherwise.

This project requires **Python 3.13+**. Pin the local interpreter with `uv python pin 3.13` if `uv run` complains about `.python-version`.

Use `python3`, not `python`, when calling the interpreter directly on macOS.

## After code changes

```bash
python3 -m compileall -q src/retarget
python3 -m compileall -q examples
pytest -q
```

`pytest` adds `src/` automatically via `pythonpath` in `pyproject.toml`. Do not require `PYTHONPATH=src` for tests.

`uv run pytest -q` is also fine.

## Demo/resampling/sync checks

```bash
pytest -q \
  tests/test_demo_resampling.py \
  tests/test_demo_contact.py \
  tests/test_demo_mocap.py \
  tests/test_demo.py \
  tests/test_demo_container.py \
  tests/test_demo_sync.py
```

## Ad-hoc `python3 -c` or scripts

```bash
PYTHONPATH=src python3 -c "from retarget.core import ..."
```

## `tests/conftest.py`

Loaded by pytest only. Not importable as `from conftest import ...` from the repo root.

Prefer `pytest -q` or `pytest -q tests/test_foo.py`.

Outside pytest: `cd tests` then `PYTHONPATH=../src python3 ...`, or use `PYTHONPATH=src:tests`.

## Examples

```bash
cd examples/process_mocap_data
PYTHONPATH=../../src:. python3 run_demo_example.py
```
